{
    "background_story": "Mac was a skilled firefighter who had seen his share of blazes, but nothing could have prepared him for the warehouse fire that would change his life forever. As he and his team responded to the emergency, the building suddenly collapsed, trapping Mac under the rubble. Despite the valiant efforts of his colleagues, he suffered severe injuries, leaving him with a permanent limp and a lifetime of PTSD. Mac's bravery and selflessness that day earned him a medal, but the true cost of his heroism was the toll it took on his body and mind. He became a casualty of the very profession he loved, a poignant reminder of the risks and sacrifices made by those who run towards danger when others flee.",
